{"diagnosis": "Fetch tb shows TRAP: no progress max_addr=0x00000000 with tohost FAIL 0xdead instead of advancing through 256-word NOP memory. mem_valid never asserts so first fetch at 0x00000000 never issues. Root cause in excerpt at picorv32.v:568 is reset assigning mem_state <= 1 instead of idle 0, parking the FSM in wait-state 1 where it waits for mem_ready that can never come while mem_valid is 0; CONE_SLICE empty so trace wins.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -566,5 +566,5 @@
 		if (!resetn || trap) begin
 			if (!resetn)
-				mem_state <= 1;
+				mem_state <= 0;
 			if (!resetn || mem_ready)
 				mem_valid <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP: no progress, max_addr > 0x00000000"}

